# NOBORU ASSETS RULE

Version: 1.0

Priority: HIGH

Status: AUTHORITATIVE

This rule governs all static and managed visual assets within Noboru.

Every illustration, icon, mascot image, achievement badge, background, audio file, UI asset, and public media file must follow this document, docs/asset-pipeline.md, and docs/asset-registry.md.

Assets are part of the product system.

Not informal file drops.

⸻

PURPOSE

The purpose of this rule is to ensure:

* Visual consistency with Noboru identity
* Traceable ownership and versioning of assets
* Predictable naming and metadata for search and reuse
* No duplicate or orphaned files in public/ or assets/
* Performance-safe delivery of media
* Long-term maintainability of the asset library

Every asset should immediately feel like Noboru.

⸻

REQUIREMENTS

References

* docs/asset-pipeline.md defines creation, review, publishing, and lifecycle
* docs/asset-registry.md defines registry entries and discoverability
* architecture.mdc ASSET PIPELINE ARCHITECTURE requires metadata, ownership, versioning, and registry entries

Naming Format

All production assets use:

category_name_variant_version

Examples:

* icon_review_check_v1.svg
* mascot_yama_happy_v2.png
* bg_region_kyoto_night_v1.webp
* achievement_streak_7day_v1.png

Rules

* lowercase
* underscore separators
* explicit version suffix
* no spaces or ambiguous abbreviations

Metadata

* Every managed asset directory or bundle requires metadata.json
* metadata.json must include at minimum:
  id
  category
  name
  variant
  version
  owner
  purpose
  format
  createdAt or versionDate
  license or source if applicable
* Registry entries must align with docs/asset-registry.md

Ownership

* Every asset has a named owner: feature, art direction, or shared system
* No anonymous assets in production paths

Versioning

* Do not overwrite production assets in place when meaningfully changed
* Increment version suffix and update metadata
* Keep deprecated assets marked in registry until safe removal

Locations

* assets/ for managed pipeline assets and source organization
* public/ for delivered static files intended for direct URL serving
* Do not place unmanaged duplicates across both trees

Performance

* Prefer modern formats such as webp or svg where appropriate
* Optimize images before production use
* Do not block core learning on decorative asset download

Educational and Brand Integrity

* Assets support learning, immersion, and progression
* Avoid generic stock visuals that break Noboru identity
* Achievement and shop assets must not imply educational advantage

⸻

CODING STANDARDS

Registry

* Register new assets in docs/asset-registry.md or approved registry system before production use
* Include feature ownership and usage locations when known

Imports

* Reference assets via stable paths or registry IDs as established by codebase conventions
* Avoid hardcoded scattered magic paths in multiple features

Metadata Files

* Keep metadata.json valid JSON
* Update version and purpose fields on change
* Document replacement relationships when superseding old assets

Public Folder Discipline

* public/ contains only intentional shipped assets
* Remove unused public assets when deprecated and registry updated

Audio and Media

* Name audio assets with same category_name_variant_version pattern
* Include duration or usage notes in metadata when helpful

⸻

SUCCESS CRITERIA

Asset work is successful when:

* Assets follow category_name_variant_version naming
* metadata.json exists and is accurate for managed assets
* Registry entries exist per docs/asset-registry.md
* No duplicate assets serve the same purpose under different names
* Visual style matches Noboru art direction
* Asset changes are versioned, not silently overwritten
* Core learning routes do not depend on unoptimized oversized media

⸻

FAILURE CRITERIA

Asset quality is degraded when any of the following occur:

* Unnamed files such as image1.png in production paths
* Missing metadata.json for managed asset groups
* Duplicate icons or backgrounds across features with different names
* In-place overwrite of versioned assets without version bump
* Orphan files in public/ with no registry entry or usage
* Assets that break mobile performance on lesson entry
* Visuals inconsistent with art direction
* Asset registry out of sync with actual files

When failure criteria appear, clean up naming and registry before adding more assets.

⸻

EXAMPLES

Correct asset path

public/icons/icon_review_check_v1.svg

Correct metadata

assets/mascots/yama/metadata.json documents mascot_yama_happy_v2.png with owner and purpose.

Correct version change

Replace mascot_yama_happy_v2.png with mascot_yama_happy_v3.png and update registry.

Incorrect naming

public/Yama Happy Final.png

Incorrect lifecycle

Editing v1 file in place after release without version increment.

Incorrect duplication

Same achievement badge copied into achievements and shop folders under different names without registry entries.

⸻

ANTI-PATTERNS

Spaces or uppercase in production filenames

Missing metadata.json in managed asset folders

Unversioned overwrite of shipped assets

Random public/ dumps after design exports

Untracked duplicate icons per feature

Huge uncompressed PNG backgrounds on mobile lesson routes

Registry entries with no actual file

Assets used before art direction or pipeline review

Hardcoded /public/foo.png paths scattered without registry IDs

Decorative assets blocking critical learning downloads

